record_count_independent_traversal=3
record_count_independence=the two counts above come from two code paths: a hand traversal of Results[] x (Vulnerabilities|Secrets|Misconfigurations) that builds no rows, and normalize.reconcile.count_records('trivy', doc). They agree, which is what makes the reconciliation identity a test rather than a restatement
records_with_multiple_locations=0
records_with_multiple_cwe_or_cve=0
records_multi_valued_selection_rule=where several CWE or CVE identifiers exist one value is selected by ascending numeric identifier (the integer after the prefix; year then sequence for CVEs). No record in this artifact is multi-valued, so the rule bound nothing here
start_line_section_dependence=present on Secrets and Misconfigurations, absent on Vulnerabilities - and verified against this artifact rather than assumed: all 3 misconfiguration records carry a CauseMetadata with Provider and Service only, so start_line is legitimately absent on every row this artifact produces
start_line_absence_permitted=true
start_line_absence_note=AAP 0.8.2 permits absence for severity_native, start_line, cwe, cve and package_coordinate only, so a vulnerability row carrying no line is legitimate rather than a rejection
unattributable_record_policy=a record that cannot be attributed to a section is rejected and counted under its own class, never guessed into one (AAP 0.1.3)
