unsupported_sections_check_method=run-trivy.sh lines 93-97 add len(res[key]) for both 'Licenses' and 'ExperimentalModifiedFindings' over every Results element of all 18 per-directory reports, and line 118 prints 'UNSUPPORTED NON-EMPTY SECTIONS PRESENT: {...}' if either is non-empty
unsupported_sections_check_evidence=two independent checks agree. (1) The runner's own check: trivy.stdout.log carries no 'UNSUPPORTED NON-EMPTY SECTIONS PRESENT' line while carrying the same block's other output at lines 32-33, so it ran to completion over this run's 18 parts. (2) This lane's check over the merged artifact itself: every Results member key was enumerated (Class, MisconfSummary, Misconfigurations, Target, Type) and neither Licenses nor ExperimentalModifiedFindings appears at all, so neither is non-empty
unsupported_sections_check_scope=all 18 per-directory reports before the merge, which is every Results element the merged artifact contains, and then the merged artifact independently
unsupported_sections_halt_triggered=false
unsupported_sections_recorded_as=an explicit boolean per unsupported section rather than an omission, because an omitted check looks identical to a passed one and the failure it guards against is real tool output silently dropped while the reconciliation identity still balances
result_member_keys_observed=Class, MisconfSummary, Misconfigurations, Target, Type
result_member_keys_all_known=true
result_member_keys_check=every Results member key was compared against normalize.adapters.trivy.RESULT_KNOWN_KEYS. A key outside that set holding a non-empty array of objects is the shape a future Trivy version's new finding section would have on its way to being dropped silently, and it halts
unsupported_sections_absent_entirely=ExperimentalModifiedFindings, Licenses
halt_check_proven_live=the check was proven to fire rather than merely to pass: copies of this artifact with a non-empty Licenses, with a non-empty ExperimentalModifiedFindings, and with an invented non-empty finding array each raised UnsupportedTrivySection from normalize.adapters.trivy.validate_finding_sections. A check that cannot fail is not a check
halt_unsupported_finding_section=not triggered
halt_unsupported_finding_section_rule=any non-empty finding array outside the three supported sections halts the run with the observed structure quoted (AAP 0.5.4, 0.9.2)
halt_nothing_distinguishing_sections=checked, not triggered
halt_nothing_distinguishing_sections_evidence=the merge preserves every section array verbatim and rewrites only Results[].Target (run-trivy.sh lines 100-109), so section membership - the sole basis for scanner_class - survives into the merged artifact
halt_nothing_distinguishing_sections_artifact_level_owner=harness/lib/normalize/adapters/trivy.py, whose halt classes unsupported_finding_section, unknown_finding_section and supported_section_not_an_array are evaluated when the artifact itself is read
