stderr_stated_reason_present=false
stderr_stated_reason_note=an empty stderr is immaterial here because the artifact was written. A tool-stated reason settles only the absent-artifact case: absent with the tool's own stated reason is recorded and the run continues, absent with none halts (AAP 0.5.4, 0.9.2)
stdout_log_reconstitution=run-trivy.sh line 60 unlinks $HARNESS_LOG_DIR/trivy.stdout.log and then appends the tool's own stdout and its per-invocation exit lines to that path, while printing its header and trailer to its own stdout. This log is those two halves in time order: the runner's stdout lines 1-13 (header through the 'invocation :' line), then what the runner appended into the file (trivy's own stdout, empty under --quiet, plus the 18 'invocation ... exit=0' lines), then the runner's stdout from 'merged ... Results sections' through 'end :'. Every byte is a real stream's; nothing is authored, and the result is 2756 bytes over 37 lines
tool_stated_reach_condition=none. trivy wrote nothing to stderr and made no statement about a scanner having nothing to resolve; the vulnerability scanner's empty result is a property of the scope, recorded here from the scope rather than quoted from the tool
artifact_absent_rule_applied=false
artifact_status_classification=present, structurally valid, all records attributable to a supported section - the 'clean' case (AAP 0.5.4). Parse status is normalization's own field and remains its measurement
artifact_status_independent_of_exit_status=asserted: the exit code is recorded as a fact and used for nothing else. A valid artifact is never suppressed because its runner exited non-zero, and a zero exit is not itself evidence about the artifact
halt_conditions_evaluated=unknown shape (not triggered), nothing distinguishing the three supported sections (not triggered), a non-empty unsupported or unknown finding section (not triggered), an artifact absent with no tool-stated reason (not applicable - the artifact is present), a runner resolving a tree other than $SPARK_SRC (not triggered), and the smoke override being set (not triggered)
manifest_owner=oss-scan-results/run-record.md publishes this file's byte size and sha256, both computed over this file after it is written; a file cannot carry its own digest without self-reference
evidence_files=harness/artifacts/logs/trivy.stdout.log, harness/artifacts/logs/trivy.stderr.log, harness/artifacts/logs/runner-metadata.json, harness/artifacts/logs/gate-record.json, harness/ENVIRONMENT.md
